<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    privoxy, the filtering HTTP proxy alpaca forwards to in macswitcher's
    direct contexts (Setup.md -> "Filtering proxy").

    An agent, not a daemon: it binds 8118 on loopback, which needs no
    privilege, and it filters this user's traffic only.

    Logging deviates from CONVENTIONS.md 2 in one visible way: there is no
    separate privoxy.err.log, and privoxy.log is written through
    StandardErrorPath rather than by the job itself.

    privoxy writes everything - startup, blocks, errors - to stderr, and its
    own `logfile` directive is honoured only when it daemonises
    (loadcfg.c:1508 gates it on daemon_mode). Under launchd it must stay in
    the foreground, so that directive is unavailable and stderr *is* the log.
    Splitting it in two would mean an empty privoxy.log next to an err.log
    holding everything, which is worse than saying so here.

    That leaves the rename problem (CONVENTIONS.md 3): privoxy holds the fd
    launchd handed it and cannot be told to reopen, because the reopen path
    (jcc.c:6259) is also gated on config->logfile being set. So rotation
    restarts it instead - etc/newsyslog.d/privoxy.conf signals the pid from
    --pidfile below with SIGTERM, and KeepAlive brings it straight back with
    a fresh fd on the new file. The cost is dropped connections at the moment
    of rotation, which at 5 MB of block-only logging is rare and cheap.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.schretzi.privoxy</string>

    <!-- --no-daemon keeps it in the foreground so launchd owns the process;
         privoxy still writes the pidfile, which is what newsyslog signals. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/sbin/privoxy</string>
        <string>--no-daemon</string>
        <string>--pidfile</string>
        <string>/Users/schretzi/.local/state/privoxy/privoxy.pid</string>
        <string>/Users/schretzi/.config/privoxy/config</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- privoxy writes nothing to stdout. -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/dev/null</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/schretzi/Library/Logs/privoxy.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
